From: Athena <root@athena>
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath11k: use byte offset for the HTT WBM completion overlay

HTT_TX_WBM_COMP_STATUS_OFFSET is a byte offset (8). The completion parser
in ath11k_dp_tx_process_htt_tx_complete() adds it to a void pointer, which
advances by bytes, and reads the overlaid HTT status word at desc + 8.
The prefilter ath11k_dp_tx_completion_valid() casts desc to
struct htt_tx_wbm_completion * first, so the same addition scales by the
16-byte struct size and reads desc + 128 instead.

When those unrelated bytes happen to decode as MEC_NOTIFY the prefilter
discards a normal firmware completion: the caller never copies the
descriptor, never retires its MSDU and never decrements num_tx_pending or
num_max_allowed. On the JDCloud RE-CS-02 both AHB radios accumulated to
8109 of the 8192 shared budget over four days, which stalls the TX path
and produces repeated "failed to flush transmit queue" warnings.

Use the same byte arithmetic as the parser so filtering and dispatch
inspect the same overlay.

---
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/dp_tx.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/dp_tx.c
@@ -839,7 +839,7 @@
 
 	if (FIELD_GET(HAL_WBM_RELEASE_INFO0_REL_SRC_MODULE, desc->info0) ==
 	    HAL_WBM_REL_SRC_MODULE_FW) {
-		status_desc = ((struct htt_tx_wbm_completion *)desc) + HTT_TX_WBM_COMP_STATUS_OFFSET;
+		status_desc = (void *)desc + HTT_TX_WBM_COMP_STATUS_OFFSET;
 
 		/* Dont consider HTT_TX_COMP_STATUS_MEC_NOTIFY */
 		if (FIELD_GET(HTT_TX_WBM_COMP_INFO0_STATUS, status_desc->info0) ==
